DESIGN GOAL:

I wanted my army to overwhelm opponents and win through total elimination. By splitting the army into three groups, I want to pressure the enemy on all three sides, creating chaos and
ruining/overpowering enemy strategies.

SHORT REFLECTION:

From the previous seasons, I found that playing around the three capture zones wasn't a good strategy. The capture zones aren't rewarding enough, and it takes too long to win by points.
Additionally, I got feedback that my army wasn't properly cooperating and was wasting turns doing nothing, so I decided to make them act faster, more efficiently, and more coordinated.
I used programming strategies like lookahead, behavioral blocks, and message communication between units. I also trained this agent against my previous agents and compared the results. That
way, I could see whether the changes were an improvement or not. I also made slight variations to this agent's strategy, like changing which units take part in the flank, and compared the results
before and after the change to figure out the best possible agent.

AI DISCLOSURE:

I used Claude Code to help with this assignment. It modified and changed a lot of code. I checked its work by reading over the code and watching the agent to see the desired results.
